Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:41:30 +0800
Subject: net: hisilicon: accept the generic FEMAC compatible


The Hi3798MV200 binding documents <"hisilicon,hi3798mv200-femac">,
<"hisilicon,hisi-femac">, so the fallback cell needs a driver entry of
its own.

Add it; the legacy -v1/-v2/hi3516cv300 strings are documented in the
same schema and stay in the table.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)


diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hisi_femac.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hisi_femac.c
index e6a13c1c9360..e1ce1aedad96 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hisi_femac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hisi_femac.c
@@ -1011,6 +1011,7 @@ static int hisi_femac_drv_resume(struct platform_device *pdev)
 #endif
 
 static const struct of_device_id hisi_femac_match[] = {
+	{.compatible = "hisilicon,hisi-femac",},
 	{.compatible = "hisilicon,hisi-femac-v1",},
 	{.compatible = "hisilicon,hisi-femac-v2",},
 	{.compatible = "hisilicon,hi3516cv300-femac",},
